\ core::show -- a fixed in-memory render buffer, a `Show['T]` trait that
\ formats a value into it, and a `Write['S]` trait that flushes it to a
\ sink. Buffer indirection (S7c R1): a value has no address to hand a
\ variadic sink (scalars have none, `cannot borrow the scalar local`), and
\ `str` cannot be constructed from computed data (only a literal or
\ `static:` produces one), so a value formats its digits into `StrBuf`
\ instead, and a separate `Write` impl (declared in the sink's own module,
\ per the orphan rule) flushes the whole buffer in one call.
\
\ This module stays `no_std`: no `extern:`, no dependency on `hosted`. The
\ actual `write(2)` sink lands in `hosted::libc` (Phase 2).

import: intrinsics * ;
import: self::bool | Bool if | ;
import: self::cmp | lt gt gte | ;
import: self::combinators | times | ;

export: StrBuf Show Write render flush ;

type: StrBuf data array[u8 64] len usize ;

trait: Show['T]
  : show ( 'T &!StrBuf -- ) ;
;

trait: Write['S]
  : write ( &!'S &!StrBuf -- ) ;
;

\ Appends one byte at the buffer's current `len`, clamped to capacity
\ (R11): a write past the last byte is discarded and `len` never exceeds
\ 64. `len` is the store index (append semantics; a fresh buffer starts at
\ `0`).
: append-byte ( &!StrBuf u8 -- )
  | buf b |
  buf &!len @ | idx |
  idx 64 >usize lt ~[
    buf &!data idx &!> b !
    buf &!len 1 +!
  ] ~[ ] if ;

\ Restoring (shift-subtract) division of a `u64` bit pattern by ten (D1):
\ integer `div` is float-only, so this walks all 64 bits from the top,
\ building the quotient one bit at a time while the running remainder
\ never exceeds the divisor. Returns `( quotient remainder )`.
: divmod10 ( u64 -- u64 u64 )
  | n |
  0 >u64 0 >u64
  64 ~[
    | i |
    | r | | q |
    63 i sub | bitpos |
    n bitpos shr 1 >u64 and | bit |
    r 1 shl bit or | r2 |
    r2 10 >u64 gte ~[
      r2 10 >u64 sub
      1 >u64 bitpos shl q or
      swap
    ] ~[
      q r2
    ] if
  ] times ;

\ Appends the decimal digits of a `u64` magnitude, most significant first,
\ via the restoring-division helper: recurse on the quotient while it is
\ still nonzero, then append the remainder -- the base case (`q = 0`)
\ appends a lone `0` for a zero magnitude instead of no digits at all.
: append-digits ( &!StrBuf u64 -- )
  | buf n |
  n divmod10 | r | | q |
  q 0 >u64 gt ~[ buf q append-digits ] ~[ ] if
  buf r >u8 48 >u8 add append-byte ;

\ Sign handling (Ruling 6): capture the sign, take the magnitude as the
\ `u64` bit pattern -- for a negative value, `>u64 not 1 >u64 add` (two's
\ complement negation over the reinterpreted bit pattern), exact even for
\ `i64::MIN`, whose magnitude does not fit back into an `i64` -- then
\ render the magnitude and prepend `-`.
impl: Show for i64
  : show
    | n buf |
    n 0 lt ~[
      buf 45 >u8 append-byte
      n >u64 not 1 >u64 add
    ] ~[
      n >u64
    ] if
    | mag |
    buf mag append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for usize
  : show
    | n buf |
    buf n >u64 append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for isize
  : show
    | n buf |
    n 0 lt ~[
      buf 45 >u8 append-byte
      n >u64 not 1 >u64 add
    ] ~[
      n >u64
    ] if
    | mag |
    buf mag append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for Bool
  : show
    | b buf |
    b ~[
      buf 116 >u8 append-byte
      buf 114 >u8 append-byte
      buf 117 >u8 append-byte
      buf 101 >u8 append-byte
    ] ~[
      buf 102 >u8 append-byte
      buf 97 >u8 append-byte
      buf 108 >u8 append-byte
      buf 115 >u8 append-byte
      buf 101 >u8 append-byte
    ] if ;
;

\ P7.S7d (R6'): the rest of the integer tower, widened onto the same
\ `append-digits` path. The signed impls widen *before* the sign test: a bare
\ `n 0 lt` on a narrow operand resolves the literal ambiguously and errors.
impl: Show for u8
  : show
    | n buf |
    buf n >u64 append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for u16
  : show
    | n buf |
    buf n >u64 append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for u32
  : show
    | n buf |
    buf n >u64 append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for u64
  : show
    | n buf |
    buf n >u64 append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for i8
  : show
    | n buf |
    n >i64 0 lt ~[
      buf 45 >u8 append-byte
      n >i64 >u64 not 1 >u64 add
    ] ~[
      n >i64 >u64
    ] if
    | mag |
    buf mag append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for i16
  : show
    | n buf |
    n >i64 0 lt ~[
      buf 45 >u8 append-byte
      n >i64 >u64 not 1 >u64 add
    ] ~[
      n >i64 >u64
    ] if
    | mag |
    buf mag append-digits ;
;

impl: Show for i32
  : show
    | n buf |
    n >i64 0 lt ~[
      buf 45 >u8 append-byte
      n >i64 >u64 not 1 >u64 add
    ] ~[
      n >i64 >u64
    ] if
    | mag |
    buf mag append-digits ;
;

\ Bounded consumer words (Ruling 8): a member name is not importable, so a
\ program reaches `show`/`write` only through one of these.
: render['T: Show] ( 'T &!StrBuf -- ) show ;
: flush['S: Write] ( &!'S &!StrBuf -- ) write ;
